---
import Gallery from '../../layouts/Gallery.astro';
import Related from '../../components/Related.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');

const markup = `<!-- BLIND by design: the expected quantity is never on screen, or
     the counter anchors to it and the count proves nothing. The one RF
     header that deliberately WITHHOLDS a number. -->
<dl class="bo-kv bo-kv--rows"> …Count doc / Bin / Item — NO expected qty… </dl>

<input class="bo-input bo-input--code" data-scan-input data-scan-flash
    aria-describedby="scan-status" />
<p id="scan-status" data-scan-status aria-live="polite" class="bo-visually-hidden"></p>

<div class="bo-quantity">
  <input class="bo-quantity__input" type="number" inputmode="numeric"
      min="0" step="1" placeholder="—" aria-label="Counted quantity" />
  <span class="bo-quantity__unit" aria-hidden="true">ea</span>
</div>

<div class="bo-btn-group bo-btn-group--bar">
  <button class="bo-btn bo-btn--secondary">Back</button>
  <button class="bo-btn bo-btn--secondary">Item not found</button>
  <button class="bo-btn">Submit count</button>
</div>`;
---
<Gallery title="Pattern: RF count">
  <p class="demo-note">
    <strong>Who uses it</strong>: whoever walks the aisles for a physical
    inventory or a cycle count. <strong>How often</strong>: cycle counts
    daily on a rotation; wall-to-wall counts a few times a year, all hands.
    <strong>What "done" looks like</strong>: the bin scanned open, what is
    ACTUALLY there entered, submitted — and critically, <strong>the
    expected quantity was never on screen</strong>. A count is blind by
    design: show the book figure and the counter anchors to it, and the
    count stops measuring reality and starts confirming the record. That
    single fact shapes this screen — it is the one RF header that
    deliberately withholds a number.
    <strong>Not for correcting a quantity you already know is wrong</strong>
    — a known discrepancy is a stock adjustment with a reason, made at a
    desk on <a href={base + '/patterns/record-detail'}>the record</a>; a
    count is how you FIND discrepancies, not how you fix them.
  </p>

  <section class="demo">
    <h2>The screen — try it</h2>
    <p>Shown the way the scanner gets it: an isolated 360×640 document
    styled by ONLY the <code>rf-essentials</code> profile
    (Chrome/WebView&nbsp;108) — not the docs bundle. One screen, not two:
    this page used to render the same component a second time at desktop
    width, which showed the reader a size no counter ever holds
    (roadmap 131.1).</p>
    <iframe
      src={base + '/patterns/rf/rf-count-rf/'}
      title="RF count, rf-essentials profile, 360×640"
      class="rf-device-frame"
    ></iframe>
    <p class="bo-u-text-muted">Scan (type + Enter) <code>C-02-08</code> to
    open the count; a wrong bin flashes the verdict. The quantity starts
    <em>empty</em>, not zero — an untouched field means "not counted yet",
    and a typed 0 means "I looked, the bin is empty": two different facts
    the record must keep apart (the same empty-vs-zero rule the timesheet
    pattern documents).</p>
  </section>

  <section class="demo">
    <h2>Markup</h2>
    <pre><code>{markup}</code></pre>
  </section>

  <section class="demo">
    <h2>Anatomy</h2>
    <ol class="bo-stack bo-stack--tight docs-list">
      <li><strong>Count header</strong> — <a href={base + '/components/kv'}>KV
        rows</a>: document + position, bin, item. No expected quantity,
        on purpose.</li>
      <li><strong>Bin scan</strong> —
        <a href={base + '/components/scan'}>scan input + flash</a>; the
        count opens only on the right bin.</li>
      <li><strong>Blind quantity</strong> —
        <a href={base + '/components/quantity'}>quantity</a>, empty until
        the counter types; the keypad recipe from
        <a href={base + '/patterns/rf-pick'}>picking</a> composes here
        unchanged.</li>
      <li><strong>Exception bar</strong> — Back / Item not found / Submit
        count.</li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="demo">
    <h2>Data contract</h2>
    <div class="bo-data-table-container" tabindex="0">
      <table class="bo-data-table" data-density="compact">
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">Request</th><th scope="col">Returns / on failure</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td class="bo-data-table__col--code">GET /rf/count/next</td><td>the next bin/item to count — WITHOUT the book quantity; blindness is enforced server-side, not by the screen's good manners</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="bo-data-table__col--code">POST /rf/count/:pos/submit</td><td>the counted figure; a large variance may return a RECOUNT of the same position (the server decides the threshold), announced as such</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="bo-data-table__col--code">POST … item-not-found</td><td>records a zero-with-reason — distinct from a typed 0, which is a counted empty bin</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="bo-data-table__col--code">409 (position already counted)</td><td>who counted it and the next position — double-counting is noise in the variance report</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="demo">
    <h2>States</h2>
    <div class="bo-data-table-container" tabindex="0">
      <table class="bo-data-table" data-density="compact">
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">State</th><th scope="col">What ships</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Awaiting bin scan</td><td>the count stays closed until the right bin opens it — counting the wrong bin is worse than not counting</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Counting</td><td>quantity empty (not zero); Submit disabled until a figure exists — empty and 0 are different facts</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Recount demanded</td><td>the same position re-opens, SAID to be a recount — a silent recount reads as a glitch and gets pencil-whipped</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Item not found</td><td>its own exception, not a typed 0 — zero-with-reason and counted-zero diverge in the variance report</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Session lost</td><td>reconnect re-renders the position as the server has it; an uncommitted count is retyped — honest, and cheaper than a wrong committed one</td></tr>
          <tr><td>No JS</td><td>scan posts on Enter, the count is a plain form; flash and steppers are enhancements</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="demo">
    <h2>Components used</h2>
    <p class="bo-u-text-muted"><span class="bo-badge">complexity 2 of 4</span></p>
    <ul class="bo-cluster docs-list-bare">
      <li><a class="bo-badge bo-badge--type" href={base + '/components/kv'}>Key-value facts</a></li>
      <li><a class="bo-badge bo-badge--type" href={base + '/components/scan'}>Scan feedback</a></li>
      <li><a class="bo-badge bo-badge--type" href={base + '/components/quantity'}>Quantity</a></li>
      <li><a class="bo-badge bo-badge--type" href={base + '/components/button'}>Button</a></li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <Related links={[
    ["/patterns/rf-pick", "RF picking (knows what it wants; a count must not)"],
    ["/patterns/rf-putaway", "RF putaway"],
    ["/patterns/rf-landing", "RF task menu"],
    ["/components/scan", "Scan feedback"],
  ]} />
</Gallery>
